nd E2 on the second line. It loses 6.2 points and the lead drops to -3.6. The engine's choice was F3, and Black never led again except for one move."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "After White's D5, Opus 5.5 plays E5 and loses 4.6 points, taking the score from -5.0 to -9.5. The engine preferred E6. This is the lowest Black's lead gets in the game, and White's stones at D4 and D5 stay strong."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "The 10k's D1 is the biggest slip on their side. It loses 9.1 points and swings the lead from -6.4 to +2.7 for Black. The engine's choice was C2, and for one move Opus 5.5 is ahead."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "Opus 5.5 answers with F1 and loses 10.4 points, sending the lead from +2.7 back to -7.8. The engine's first choice was C2, which White takes on the very next move. From here to the final passes no move loses more than 0.3 points, so this is where the game was decided."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a board given on stdin and prints each group's stones and liberties for the current position, with no candidate generation or look-ahead. The other commands were cat/tail of games.md and appending a game log to it, which is record keeping.", "stop": false}}